// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'Join'. Valid alternatives: ['Table', 'View', 'TabularFunction', ')']
//
// A Schema may contain only Table, View and TabularFunction. Join, Filter and
// MultiGrainFilter are Database-level only -- they can reference schema-qualified columns
// (`s.T.ID`) but they may not be nested inside the Schema that owns those columns.
//
// The pull towards permissiveness here is strong: a Join written next to the tables it
// joins reads better than one hoisted to the top, and a parser that reuses one
// "database-element" routine for both bodies allows it. Doing so would accept a Database
// whose joins legend-engine cannot even parse.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::JoinInSchema
(
   Schema s
   (
      Join TU(s.T.OTHER_ID = s.U.ID)
      Table T (ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY, OTHER_ID VARCHAR(32))
   )
)
